é500,40,1,0,Where's the meat?é

èNasreddin Hodja sometimes brought meat home, but never had the chance to eat it.è

èHis wife either ate it herself or shared it with her friends, always offering the same excuse;è

è"The cat got it, I couldn't stop her."è

èOne day Nasreddin Hodja brought two kilos of meat home and gave it to his wife to cook.è

èAt dinnertime when his wife gave him the same excuse, he took the cat and put it on the scales.è

èThe cat weighed exactly two kilos.è

è"Woman"- he said-" if this is the cat, where's the meat? And if this is the meat, where's the cat?è

